From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aoc_channel_dev: don't take the list head as the doorbell channel

aocc_sh_mem_doorbell_probe() picks the first channel device with
list_entry(aocc_devices_list.next, ...). When usf_sh_mem_doorbell probes
before any channel service, the list is empty and that yields the list
head itself (never NULL), so the doorbell setup then writes
sh_mem_doorbell_count/available and INIT_WORK into static memory next to
aocc_devices_list. Use list_first_entry_or_null(). The setup is retried
on every probe, so it still happens once a channel shows up.

Needed for the USF sensor hub (/dev/acd-com.google.usf).

Local only, not for upstream submission.
---
--- a/aoc/aoc_channel_dev.c	2026-10-10 16:22:50.387795388 -0500
+++ b/aoc/aoc_channel_dev.c	2026-10-10 16:22:50.389278234 -0500
@@ -737,8 +737,12 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Use the first channel device with the shared memory doorbell. */
+	/*
+	 * list_entry() on an empty list returns the list head itself, which
+	 * is not NULL; the doorbell service can probe before any channel.
+	 */
 	sh_mem_doorbell_channel_device =
-		list_entry(aocc_devices_list.next, struct aocc_device_entry, list);
+		list_first_entry_or_null(&aocc_devices_list, struct aocc_device_entry, list);
 
 	/*
 	 * If both a shared memory doorbell service device and a channel device
